<h2 id="hunter">5. Jaguars: Travis Hunter's Return to Full Speed</h2>
<p>Jacksonville's most important camp storyline isn't really a competition between two players — it's whether Travis Hunter can return to the explosive form that made him a two-way sensation as a rookie before a torn LCL cut his season short. Hunter is fully cleared for camp and will work primarily at cornerback while still factoring into the receiver rotation. With the Jaguars deeper at receiver than cornerback, how close Hunter's practice-field speed and change of direction are to his pre-injury level will shape how the coaching staff builds the defensive backfield around him.</p>
<h2 id="why">Why Athleticism Decides These Battles</h2>
<p>Most camp competitions are close calls on tape — two players who look similar on paper, decided by chemistry, scheme familiarity, or a coach's gut feel. The battles above are different because the deciding factor is measurable: closing speed, burst out of a cut, straight-line recovery. Those are exactly the traits that show up in testing numbers long before a single preseason snap is played, which is why the combine and pro day numbers on these players are worth revisiting as camp reports roll in over the next few weeks.</p>
