<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">What makes a camp battle "athleticism-decided" versus scheme-decided?</div>
<div class="faq-a">A scheme-decided battle usually comes down to which player's skill set fits what the coordinator wants to run. An athleticism-decided battle is one where the players are relatively similar schematically, and the tiebreaker is a measurable trait — speed, burst, or explosiveness — that shows up directly in practice reps.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How much do preseason snaps actually predict regular season roles?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Preseason usage is a meaningful signal but not a guarantee. Coaches often use August reps to evaluate depth pieces broadly, so a strong camp doesn't always translate directly into Week 1 playing time — but a player who's clearly winning 1-on-1 reps in camp is very likely to see an expanded role once the season starts.</div>
